+To progressively enhance the design for larger screens using CSS media queries while prioritizing the mobile experience, we start with a "mobile-first" approach. This means we define the base styles for small screens first and then use media queries to add enhancements for tablets and desktops.
+
+Here is the complete HTML and CSS code for a responsive webpage:
+
+```html
+<!DOCTYPE html>
+<html lang="en">
+<head>
+  <meta charset="UTF-8">
+  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
+  <title>Responsive Design with Media Queries</title>
+  <style>
+    /* Base styles for mobile-first design */
+    body {
+      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
+      margin: 0;
+      padding: 0;
+      line-height: 1.6;
+      color: #333;
+      background-color: #f9f9f9;
