+To polish the UI for the URL Shortening Service, we can use a React frontend to create a user-friendly interface. This interface will allow users to shorten URLs, access analytics, and redirect to the original URLs seamlessly. We'll use Tailwind CSS for styling to ensure a clean, modern design.
+
+Below is the complete React code for the frontend:
+
+### Features:
+1. **Input Form**: Users can input a long URL to generate a shortened URL.
+2. **Generated Short URL**: Display the shortened URL with a "Copy" button.
+3. **Analytics Section**: Show the number of visits and original URL for a given short URL.
+4. **Styling**: Use Tailwind CSS for a polished appearance with responsive design.
+
+### React Code
+```javascript
+import React, { useState } from "react";
+
+const App = () => {
+  const [originalURL, setOriginalURL] = useState("");
+  const [shortURL, setShortURL] = useState("");
+  const [analytics, setAnalytics] = useState(null);
+  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false);
+  const [error, setError] = useState("");
+
+  const handleShorten = async () => {
+    setError("");
+    setLoading(true);
+    try {
+      const response = await fetch("http://localhost:3000/shorten", {
+        method: "POST",
+        headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
+        body: JSON.stringify({ originalURL }),
+      });
+      const data = await response.json();
+      if (response.ok) {
+        setShortURL(`http://localhost:3000/${data.shortURL}`);
+        setAnalytics(null); // Clear previous analytics
+      } else {
+        setError(data.error || "Failed to shorten URL.");
+      }
+    } catch (err) {
+      setError("Error connecting to the server.");
+    }
+    setLoading(false);
+  };
+
+  const handleFetchAnalytics = async () => {
+    setError("");
+    setLoading(true);
+    try {
+      const shortKey = shortURL.split("/").pop();
+      const response = await fetch(`http://localhost:3000/analytics/${shortKey}`);
+      const data = await response.json();
+      if (response.ok) {
+        setAnalytics(data);
+      } else {
+        setError(data.error || "Failed to fetch analytics.");
+      }
+    } catch (err) {
+      setError("Error connecting to the server.");
+    }
+    setLoading(false);
+  };
+
+  return (
+    <div className="min-h-screen bg-gray-100 flex flex-col items-center justify-center p-4">
+      <div className="bg-white shadow-md rounded-lg p-6 w-full max-w-md">
+        <h1 className="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4 text-center">
+          URL Shortener
+        </h1>
+        <div className="mb-4">
+          <label className="block text-gray-700 font-medium mb-2">
+            Enter a URL to shorten:
+          </label>
+          <input
+            type="text"
+            value={originalURL}
+            onChange={(e) => setOriginalURL(e.target.value)}
+            placeholder="https://example.com"
+            className="w-full px-4 py-2 border border-gray-300 rounded-lg focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-blue-500"
+          />
+        </div>
+        <button
+          onClick={handleShorten}
+          disabled={loading || !originalURL}
+          className={`w-full py-2 rounded-lg text-white ${
+            loading
+              ? "bg-blue-300 cursor-not-allowed"
+              : "bg-blue-500 hover:bg-blue-600"
+          }`}
+        >
+          {loading ? "Shortening..." : "Shorten URL"}
+        </button>
+        {error && (
+          <p className="text-red-500 text-sm mt-2">{error}</p>
+        )}
+        {shortURL && (
+          <div className="mt-4 p-4 bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg">
+            <p className="text-gray-800 font-medium">
+              Shortened URL:
+            </p>
+            <div className="flex items-center mt-2">
+              <a
+                href={shortURL}
+                target="_blank"
+                rel="noopener noreferrer"
+                className="text-blue-500 underline truncate"
+              >
+                {shortURL}
+              </a>
+              <button
+                onClick={() => navigator.clipboard.writeText(shortURL)}
+                className="ml-4 px-3 py-1 bg-green-500 text-white text-sm rounded-lg hover:bg-green-600"
+              >
+                Copy
+              </button>
+            </div>
+          </div>
+        )}
+      </div>
+      {shortURL && (
+        <div className="bg-white shadow-md rounded-lg p-6 w-full max-w-md mt-6">
+          <h2 className="text-xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4">
+            Analytics
+          </h2>
+          <button
+            onClick={handleFetchAnalytics}
+            disabled={loading}
+            className={`w-full py-2 rounded-lg text-white ${
+              loading
+                ? "bg-blue-300 cursor-not-allowed"
+                : "bg-blue-500 hover:bg-blue-600"
+            }`}
+          >
+            {loading ? "Fetching..." : "Fetch Analytics"}
+          </button>
+          {analytics && (
+            <div className="mt-4">
+              <p className="text-gray-800 font-medium">
+                Original URL:
+              </p>
+              <p className="text-gray-600 truncate">
+                {analytics.originalURL}
+              </p>
+              <p className="text-gray-800 font-medium mt-2">
+                Total Visits:
+              </p>
+              <p className="text-gray-600">{analytics.visits}</p>
+            </div>
+          )}
+        </div>
+      )}
+    </div>
+  );
+};
+
+export default App;
+```
+
+### Features of the UI:
+1. **Input Validation**: Ensures the user enters a URL before submitting.
+2. **Loading States**: Provides visual feedback when an action is in progress (e.g., "Shortening..." or "Fetching...").
+3. **Error Handling**: Displays error messages if the server is unreachable or if the input is invalid.
+4. **Copy to Clipboard**: Allows users to copy the shortened URL with a single click.
+5. **Responsive Design**: The layout adjusts for smaller screens using Tailwind's responsive utilities.
+
+### Styling with Tailwind:
+- **Colors**: Used a blue primary color for buttons and links, and a green color for the copy button.
+- **Spacing**: Added padding and margins for proper spacing between elements.
+- **Rounded Corners**: Applied `rounded-lg` to create a modern, soft look.
+- **Hover Effects**: Buttons change color slightly on hover to provide a better user experience.
+
+### How to Run:
+1. Set up the backend Node.js server as described in the previous step.
+2. Create a React project using `npx create-react-app url-shortener-ui` or equivalent.
+3. Replace the `App.js` file in your React project with the above code.
+4. Install Tailwind CSS in your React project using the [official guide](https://tailwindcss.com/docs/installation).
+5. Start the React app with `npm start`.
+
+With this polished UI, users will have an intuitive and pleasant experience interacting with the URL Shortening Service.
