+To enhance the existing drag-and-drop tool by allowing users to name and save multiple different layouts, we'll introduce the following features:
+
+1. **Save Multiple Layouts:** Users can save the current layout with a unique name.
+2. **Load Saved Layouts:** Users can view a list of saved layouts and load any of them.
+3. **Delete Layouts:** Users can delete unwanted saved layouts.
+
+**Solution Overview:**
+
+1. **State Management:**
+   - **`availableComponents`**: List of predefined components available in the palette.
+   - **`layoutComponents`**: Current layout components.
+   - **`savedLayouts`**: An object storing multiple layouts with their respective names.
+   - **`newLayoutName`**: Stores the name input for saving a new layout.
+
+2. **Local Storage Handling:**
+   - **Saving Layouts**: Saves the `savedLayouts` object to `localStorage`.
+   - **Loading Layouts**: Retrieves the `savedLayouts` from `localStorage` on component mount.
+
+3. **UI Enhancements:**
+   - **Save Layout Section**: Input field to name the layout and a button to save it.
+   - **Saved Layouts List**: Displays all saved layouts with options to load or delete each layout.
+
+4. **Drag-and-Drop Functionality:**
+   - Remains largely the same, allowing users to drag components from the palette to the layout area and rearrange them.
+
+**External Libraries Used:**
+- `react-beautiful-dnd`: For implementing drag-and-drop functionality.
+- `uuid`: To generate unique IDs for each component instance.
+
+**Installation Commands:**
+Before running the code, ensure you install the necessary dependencies:
+```bash
+npm install react-beautiful-dnd uuid
+```
+
+**Code Implementation:**
+
+```javascript
+import React, { useState, useEffect } from 'react';
+import { DragDropContext, Droppable, Draggable } from 'react-beautiful-dnd';
+import { v4 as uuidv4 } from 'uuid';
+
+// Predefined components
+const COMPONENTS = [
+  { id: '1', content: 'Header' },
+  { id: '2', content: 'Button' },
+  { id: '3', content: 'Image' },
+];
+
+const DragAndDropBuilder = () => {
+  const [availableComponents] = useState(COMPONENTS);
+  const [layoutComponents, setLayoutComponents] = useState([]);
+  const [savedLayouts, setSavedLayouts] = useState({});
+  const [newLayoutName, setNewLayoutName] = useState('');
+
+  // Load saved layouts from localStorage on mount
+  useEffect(() => {
+    const saved = localStorage.getItem('savedLayouts');
+    if (saved) {
+      setSavedLayouts(JSON.parse(saved));
+    }
+
+    const savedCurrentLayout = localStorage.getItem('currentLayout');
+    if (savedCurrentLayout) {
+      setLayoutComponents(JSON.parse(savedCurrentLayout));
+    }
+  }, []);
+
+  // Save current layout to localStorage whenever it changes
+  useEffect(() => {
+    localStorage.setItem('currentLayout', JSON.stringify(layoutComponents));
+  }, [layoutComponents]);
+
+  // Function to handle drag end
+  const onDragEnd = (result) => {
+    const { source, destination } = result;
+
+    // Dropped outside a droppable area
+    if (!destination) return;
+
+    // Dragging from palette to layout
+    if (source.droppableId === 'palette' && destination.droppableId === 'layout') {
+      const component = availableComponents[source.index];
+      const newComponent = { ...component, uniqueId: uuidv4() };
+      const newLayout = Array.from(layoutComponents);
+      newLayout.splice(destination.index, 0, newComponent);
+      setLayoutComponents(newLayout);
+      return;
+    }
+
+    // Rearranging within layout
+    if (source.droppableId === 'layout' && destination.droppableId === 'layout') {
+      const newLayout = Array.from(layoutComponents);
+      const [movedComponent] = newLayout.splice(source.index, 1);
+      newLayout.splice(destination.index, 0, movedComponent);
+      setLayoutComponents(newLayout);
+      return;
+    }
+
+    // Prevent dragging between palette and layout
+    return;
+  };
+
+  // Function to save the current layout with a name
+  const saveCurrentLayout = () => {
+    if (!newLayoutName.trim()) {
+      alert('Please enter a valid layout name.');
+      return;
+    }
+
+    if (savedLayouts[newLayoutName]) {
+      if (!window.confirm('A layout with this name already exists. Overwrite?')) {
+        return;
+      }
+    }
+
+    const updatedSavedLayouts = {
+      ...savedLayouts,
+      [newLayoutName]: layoutComponents,
+    };
+
+    setSavedLayouts(updatedSavedLayouts);
+    localStorage.setItem('savedLayouts', JSON.stringify(updatedSavedLayouts));
+    setNewLayoutName('');
+    alert('Layout saved successfully!');
+  };
+
+  // Function to load a saved layout
+  const loadLayout = (name) => {
+    const layout = savedLayouts[name];
+    if (layout) {
+      setLayoutComponents(layout);
+    }
+  };
+
+  // Function to delete a saved layout
+  const deleteLayout = (name) => {
+    if (window.confirm(`Are you sure you want to delete the layout "${name}"?`)) {
+      const updatedSavedLayouts = { ...savedLayouts };
+      delete updatedSavedLayouts[name];
+      setSavedLayouts(updatedSavedLayouts);
+      localStorage.setItem('savedLayouts', JSON.stringify(updatedSavedLayouts));
+    }
+  };
+
+  // Function to render components based on their type
+  const renderComponent = (component) => {
+    switch (component.content) {
+      case 'Header':
+        return <h2 className="text-2xl font-bold">Header Component</h2>;
+      case 'Button':
+        return <button className="px-4 py-2 bg-blue-500 text-white rounded">Button Component</button>;
+      case 'Image':
+        return <img src="/api/placeholder/200/150" alt="placeholder" className="w-48 h-36 object-cover" />;
+      default:
+        return <div>Unknown Component</div>;
+    }
+  };
+
+  return (
+    <div className="flex h-screen">
+      {/* Palette */}
+      <div className="w-1/4 p-4 bg-gray-100">
+        <h3 className="text-lg font-semibold mb-4">Components Palette</h3>
+        <DragDropContext onDragEnd={onDragEnd}>
+          <Droppable droppableId="palette" isDropDisabled={true}>
+            {(provided) => (
+              <div {...provided.droppableProps} ref={provided.innerRef}>
+                {availableComponents.map((component, index) => (
+                  <Draggable key={component.id} draggableId={component.id} index={index}>
+                    {(providedDrag) => (
+                      <div
+                        ref={providedDrag.innerRef}
+                        {...providedDrag.draggableProps}
+                        {...providedDrag.dragHandleProps}
+                        className="mb-2 p-2 bg-white border rounded shadow-sm cursor-grab"
+                      >
+                        {component.content}
+                      </div>
+                    )}
+                  </Draggable>
+                ))}
+                {provided.placeholder}
+              </div>
+            )}
+          </Droppable>
+        </DragDropContext>
+      </div>
+
+      {/* Layout Area */}
+      <div className="w-3/4 p-4 flex flex-col">
+        <div className="flex justify-between items-start mb-4">
+          <div>
+            <h3 className="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Layout Area</h3>
+            <DragDropContext onDragEnd={onDragEnd}>
+              <Droppable droppableId="layout">
+                {(provided) => (
+                  <div
+                    className="min-h-full p-4 bg-gray-50 border border-dashed rounded"
+                    {...provided.droppableProps}
+                    ref={provided.innerRef}
+                  >
+                    {layoutComponents.map((component, index) => (
+                      <Draggable key={component.uniqueId} draggableId={component.uniqueId} index={index}>
+                        {(providedDrag) => (
+                          <div
+                            ref={providedDrag.innerRef}
+                            {...providedDrag.draggableProps}
+                            {...providedDrag.dragHandleProps}
+                            className="mb-4 p-4 bg-white border rounded shadow"
+                          >
+                            {renderComponent(component)}
+                          </div>
+                        )}
+                      </Draggable>
+                    ))}
+                    {provided.placeholder}
+                    {layoutComponents.length === 0 && (
+                      <p className="text-gray-500">Drag components here to build your layout.</p>
+                    )}
+                  </div>
+                )}
+              </Droppable>
+            </DragDropContext>
+          </div>
+
+          {/* Save Layout Section */}
+          <div className="w-1/3 ml-4">
+            <h3 className="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Save Current Layout</h3>
+            <input
+              type="text"
+              value={newLayoutName}
+              onChange={(e) => setNewLayoutName(e.target.value)}
+              placeholder="Enter layout name"
+              className="w-full p-2 mb-2 border rounded"
+            />
+            <button
+              onClick={saveCurrentLayout}
+              className="w-full px-4 py-2 bg-green-500 text-white rounded hover:bg-green-600"
+            >
+              Save Layout
+            </button>
+
+            {/* Saved Layouts List */}
+            <div className="mt-6">
+              <h3 className="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Saved Layouts</h3>
+              {Object.keys(savedLayouts).length === 0 && (
+                <p className="text-gray-500">No layouts saved yet.</p>
+              )}
+              {Object.keys(savedLayouts).map((name) => (
+                <div key={name} className="flex items-center justify-between mb-2 p-2 bg-white border rounded shadow-sm">
+                  <span>{name}</span>
+                  <div className="flex space-x-2">
+                    <button
+                      onClick={() => loadLayout(name)}
+                      className="px-2 py-1 bg-blue-500 text-white rounded hover:bg-blue-600"
+                    >
+                      Load
+                    </button>
+                    <button
+                      onClick={() => deleteLayout(name)}
+                      className="px-2 py-1 bg-red-500 text-white rounded hover:bg-red-600"
+                    >
+                      Delete
+                    </button>
+                  </div>
+                </div>
+              ))}
+            </div>
+          </div>
+        </div>
+
+        {/* Optionally, you can add a footer or additional controls here */}
+      </div>
+    </div>
+  );
+};
+
+export default DragAndDropBuilder;
+```
+
+**Explanation of the Enhanced Code:**
+
+1. **State Variables:**
+   - **`savedLayouts`**: An object where each key is a layout name, and the value is the array of layout components.
+   - **`newLayoutName`**: Stores the name input by the user for saving a new layout.
+
+2. **Local Storage Handling:**
+   - **Loading Saved Layouts:** On component mount (`useEffect`), the code retrieves `savedLayouts` and `currentLayout` from `localStorage` if they exist.
+   - **Saving Layouts:** Whenever the layout changes, it's saved to `localStorage` under `currentLayout`.
+   - **Saving Multiple Layouts:** When a user saves a layout, it's added to the `savedLayouts` state and persisted in `localStorage`.
+
+3. **Save Layout Functionality:**
+   - **`saveCurrentLayout`**: Validates the layout name, checks for duplicates, and saves the current layout under the provided name. If a layout with the same name exists, it prompts the user for confirmation before overwriting.
+
+4. **Load Layout Functionality:**
+   - **`loadLayout`**: Loads a selected saved layout into the `layoutComponents` state, effectively updating the layout area.
+
+5. **Delete Layout Functionality:**
+   - **`deleteLayout`**: Removes a selected layout from `savedLayouts` after user confirmation and updates `localStorage`.
+
+6. **UI Enhancements:**
+   - **Save Layout Section:** Positioned next to the layout area, it includes an input field for the layout name and a button to save the layout.
+   - **Saved Layouts List:** Displays all saved layouts with "Load" and "Delete" buttons for each. This allows users to manage their saved layouts efficiently.
+
+7. **Styling:**
+   - Tailwind CSS classes are consistently used to ensure a clean and responsive design.
+   - Buttons have hover effects for better user interaction feedback.
+
+8. **Drag-and-Drop Functionality:**
+   - Remains consistent with the previous implementation, allowing users to drag components from the palette to the layout area and rearrange them as needed.
+
+This enhanced implementation provides a more flexible and user-friendly interface, enabling users to manage multiple layouts effectively. Users can now create, save, load, and delete various layouts, enhancing the tool's utility and versatility.
+
